From: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 09:24:38 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] mm/migrate_device: allocate deferred split sublists for new
 huge folios

migrate_vma_insert_huge_pmd_page() can populate an anonymous mapping
with a newly charged large folio. Unlike the normal anonymous THP
allocation paths, it does not allocate the charged memcg's deferred
split sublist.

If the memcg has no sublist, partially unmapping the folio makes
deferred_split_folio() fall back to an ancestor's list. This warns
because the fallback is intended for dying cgroups. If a subsequent
normal THP allocation creates the missing sublist, freeing the earlier
folio removes it from the ancestor's list while holding the child's
lock and updating the child's count. The accounting is then wrong,
and concurrent deferred split scanning can corrupt the list. A
DEBUG_LIST-enabled pre-patch kernel reported list_del corruption in
__folio_unqueue_deferred_split() in two guest runs; one warning occurred
during a timed scan/removal trial. Kernel crashes or hangs are possible,
but neither was observed in these runs.

The list_lru conversion added sublist allocation to anonymous faults,
swapin and collapse, but missed this path, which creates new folios
rather than merely transferring an existing charge during migration.

Allocate the deferred split sublist after charging and before installing
the PMD. On failure, use the existing abort path to clear the migration
flags and leave the destination folio for migration finalization to
release. Count this as an allocation fallback rather than a memcg
charge failure.

Fixes: fafaeceb89a5 ("mm: switch deferred split shrinker to list_lru")
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Reported-by: Ada Smith <adasmithgt@gmail.com>
Tested-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: Jason Gunthorpe <jgg@ziepe.ca>
Cc: David Hildenbrand <david@kernel.org>
Cc: Johannes Weiner <hannes@cmpxchg.org>
Cc: Balbir Singh <balbirs@nvidia.com>
Cc: Alistair Popple <apopple@nvidia.com>
Cc: Zi Yan <ziy@nvidia.com>
Cc: Shakeel Butt <shakeel.butt@linux.dev>
Cc: <stable@kernel.org>
---
 mm/migrate_device.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mm/migrate_device.c b/mm/migrate_device.c
index 9e19fadfa65c6..7919e04abc1c5 100644
--- a/mm/migrate_device.c
+++ b/mm/migrate_device.c
@@ -833,6 +833,13 @@ static int migrate_vma_insert_huge_pmd_page(struct migrate_vma *migrate,
 		goto abort;
 	}
 
+	/* The charged memcg needs its own sublist before deferred splitting. */
+	if (folio_memcg_alloc_deferred(folio)) {
+		count_vm_event(THP_FAULT_FALLBACK);
+		count_mthp_stat(HPAGE_PMD_ORDER, MTHP_STAT_ANON_FAULT_FALLBACK);
+		goto abort;
+	}
+
 	__folio_mark_uptodate(folio);
 
 	pgtable = pte_alloc_one(vma->vm_mm);
-- 
